@startuml pricing-service-database-schema

!define Table(name,desc) class name as "desc" << (T,#FFAAAA) >>
!define primary_key(x) <b><u>x</u></b>
!define foreign_key(x) <i>x</i>
!define unique(x) <color:blue>x</color>

title Pricing Service Database Schema (pricing-db)

Table(pricing_rules, "pricing_rules") {
  primary_key(id): BIGSERIAL
  --
  item_id: BIGINT NOT NULL
  store_id: BIGINT
  price: DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL
  valid_from: DATE
  valid_to: DATE
  created_at: TIMESTAMP
  updated_at: TIMESTAMP
  created_by: BIGINT
  --
  Indexes:
  idx_pricing_rules_item_store (item_id, store_id)
  idx_pricing_rules_validity (valid_from, valid_to)
  --
  Unique Constraint:
  UNIQUE(item_id, store_id, valid_from)
}

Table(product_points_rules, "product_points_rules") {
  primary_key(id): BIGSERIAL
  --
  unique(item_id): BIGINT NOT NULL
  points_per_unit: DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 1.0
  created_at: TIMESTAMP
  updated_at: TIMESTAMP
}

note right of pricing_rules
  **Hierarchical Pricing:**
  - store_id = NULL: Global rule (Network Manager)
  - store_id = <id>: Store-specific override (Store/Network Manager)
  
  **Rule Precedence:**
  1. Store-specific rule (if exists)
  2. Global rule (fallback)
  3. Warehouse catalog price (final fallback)
  
  **Validity Period:**
  - valid_from/valid_to: Optional date range
  - NULL = always valid
  - Checked against current date during calculation
  
  **References (not enforced):**
  - item_id → warehouse.items.id (legacy MySQL)
  - store_id → stores.id (Store Service)
  - created_by → users.id (Auth Service)
end note

note right of product_points_rules
  **Loyalty Points Configuration:**
  - Network Manager sets points earned per unit
  - Default: 1.0 point per unit
  - Used by Loyalty Service for points calculation
  
  **References (not enforced):**
  - item_id → warehouse.items.id (legacy MySQL)
end note

@enduml
